      "mechanic_id": "DATA_FIELDS",
      "bucket": "character_progression",
      "text": "This directory contains the C# implementations of the MajorBBS/Worldgroup SDK libraries. When a loaded module's x86 code executes a `CALL FAR` to a virtual segment (>= 0xFF00), the CPU fires `_invokeExternalFunctionDelegate`, which routes to the appropriate exported module's `Invoke(ordinal)` method. These classes are the bridge between the emulated 16-bit world and modern C#."
    },
    {
      "source": "MBBSEmu",
      "priority": 3,
      "path": "MBBSEmu/MBBSEmu-master/MBBSEmu/HostProcess/ExportedModules/CLAUDE.md",
      "line": 14,
      "mechanic_id": "ITEM_EFFECTS",
      "bucket": "character_progression",
      "text": "| `Doscalls.cs` | ~175 | OS/2-style DOS calls: DosAllocSeg, DosLoadModule, DosGetProcAddr, DosGetModHandle |"
    },
    {
      "source": "MBBSEmu",
      "priority": 3,
      "path": "MBBSEmu/MBBSEmu-master/MBBSEmu/HostProcess/ExportedModules/CLAUDE.md",
      "line": 75,
      "mechanic_id": "DATA_FIELDS",
      "bucket": "character_progression",
      "text": "**Important**: Pointer parameters consume 2 ordinal slots (offset + segment). So if param 0 is a pointer, the next scalar is at ordinal 2, not 1."
    },
    {
      "source": "MBBSEmu",
      "priority": 3,
      "path": "MBBSEmu/MBBSEmu-master/MBBSEmu/HostProcess/ExportedModules/CLAUDE.md",
      "line": 94,
      "mechanic_id": "ITEM_EFFECTS",
      "bucket": "character_progression",
      "text": "- Btrieve helpers: `BtrieveSaveProcessor()`, `BtrieveGetProcessor()`, `BtrieveDeleteProcessor()`, `BtrieveSetupGlobalPointer()`"
    },
    {
      "source": "MBBSEmu",
      "priority": 3,
      "path": "MBBSEmu/MBBSEmu-master/MBBSEmu/HostProcess/ExportedModules/CLAUDE.md",
      "line": 137,
      "mechanic_id": "ITEM_EFFECTS",
      "bucket": "character_progression",
      "text": "**Properties** (Phase 1) return a 4-byte `ReadOnlySpan<byte>` containing a `FarPtr` that points to the variable's location in module memory. These are used by the NE relocation process \u2014 the loader patches the module's code with the returned address."
